WEBVTT

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.570
OHMA TOKITA - FIGHTER
YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.450
<i>Ohma Tokita,</i>

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.210
<i>you are weak.</i>

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.630
<i>Raian Kure is strong.</i>

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.500
<i>No matter how hard you try,</i>
<i>you don't stand a chance.</i>

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:53.880
Damn it!

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:02.640
His phantom again!

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.850
It seems you're unable to hit me
since I'm like a father figure to you.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.900
NIKO TOKITA
OHMA'S MASTER OF NIKO STYLE

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.110
What do you want?

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.280
You may not ask for it,

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:20.120
but as your master,
I'll tell you why you're weak.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:25.210
You don't trust your own martial art.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:30.460
That's why you have doubt
and lose your agility.

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:35.840
Do you really think you can be strong
without trusting your techniques?

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.300
I wanted to be strong.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.720
Stronger than anyone!

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.140
<i>That's why I learned your Niko Style.</i>

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.020
But you lost!

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.230
You lost and died!

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:58.070
How can I trust the techniques
learned from someone weak like you?

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:00.700
Right.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:03.370
With my Niko Style,

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.000
<i>you might not be able to win</i>
<i>against the son of Kure.</i>

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.940
THE ABYSS

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.530
F. KURE
KURE FAMILY, RAIAN'S YOUNGER SISTER

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.540
KENZO YAMASHITA- KAZUO'S OLDEST SON -

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.210
It's finally begun.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.960
<i>Thank you for waiting!</i>

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:20.050
It's time to start the second stage of
the Kengan Life-or-Death Tournament!

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:22.090
SAYAKA KATAHARA
DAUGHTER OF METSUDO KATAHARA

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:28.760
ADAM DUDLEY
(ELIMINATED)

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:31.730
-Don't lose to an effing cop!
-Go, Cos!

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:33.810
AKIRA NISHIHONJI
NISHIHONJI SECURITY SERVICES

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.020
COSMO IMAI, REP. FIGHTER

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.230
Thanks, guys.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.940
I'm sure I'll win!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:46.160
<i>That kid grew up even stronger</i>
<i>than I could have expected.</i>

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:50.910
<i>You accepted a pupil?</i>

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.790
<i>Yeah, a man like me</i>
<i>happened to be a teacher.</i>

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.330
<i>He's still an amateur,</i>
<i>but if I guide him well...</i>

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.750
MITSUYO KUREISHI, MMA FIGHTER

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.630
<i>...he could be an interesting</i>
<i>martial arts fighter.</i>

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.340
-Cosmo!
-Yes!

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.010
<i>This is Nishihonji,</i>

00:05:09.550 --> 00:05:11.770
<i>a junior of mine at my previous gym.</i>

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.430
<i>Oh, yeah?</i>

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:15.520
<i>He's your junior?</i>

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:19.360
<i>I guess that means he's my senior, right?</i>

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.900
<i>Nice to meet you, Mr. Nishihonji.</i>

00:05:27.280 --> 00:05:30.830
<i>The fighters of the first game</i>
<i>are making their entrances!</i>

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:32.200
KENGAN MATCH

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:40.250
<i>Same as the opening match, his smile gives</i>
<i>the second stage a sparkling beginning!</i>

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.340
GAME 1

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.210
<i>But be careful,</i>
<i>for he isn't just good-looking.</i>

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:49.430
In the match against Adam "the Emperor"
Dudley, who has an outstanding body trunk,

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:53.430
<i>he won by choking him despite</i>
<i>a difference of 40 kg in body weight.</i>

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.230
<i>No one doubts</i>
<i>his ground grappling techniques!</i>

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:00.400
<i>Standing at 171 cm and weighing 68 kg,</i>

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.570
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>22 wins and no losses.</i>

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:10.120
Total assets he acquired is
79 billion 212 million yen.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.870
Representing Nishihonji Security Services,

00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:16.830
<i>also known as the King of Stranglers,</i>

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:21.540
<i>Cosmo Imai!</i>

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.270
Good luck, Akoya.

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.940
Luck?

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:42.810
That word is only needed by weak people.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:45.610
My victory is obvious.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.700
Justice never fails.

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:50.780
VERSUS

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:54.580
<i>This man was strong in a battle</i>
<i>without support from the state.</i>

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:58.540
<i>In his first match, there was</i>
<i>a 200 kg weight difference!</i>

00:06:58.910 --> 00:07:03.790
His opponent Haruo Kohno, also known as
the Destroyer, was destroyed by him!

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:08.380
<i>Is the key to his victory</i>
<i>his invisibly fast reflexes?</i>

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:12.720
<i>Or his eccentric faith in justice?</i>

00:07:13.010 --> 00:07:16.890
<i>Standing at 191 cm and weighing 114 kg,</i>

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:21.310
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>40 wins and no losses.</i>

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:27.780
Total assets he acquired is
191,115,000,000 yen.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.200
Representing
Wakasa Life Insurance Company,

00:07:30.820 --> 00:07:32.860
<i>also known as the Executioner,</i>

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:36.990
<i>Seishu Akoya!</i>

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.460
SEISHU AKOYA - FIGHTER
WAKASA LIFE INSURANCE COMPANY

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:53.220
<i>In contrast to Imai, he's going</i>
<i>to fight in his martial arts uniform.</i>

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:55.220
I watched your first round.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.720
You're an amazing kengan fighter.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:02.140
I'm really excited about fighting
a strong guy like you.

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:06.310
<i>Let's see who will advance</i>
<i>to the third stage.</i>

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.230
<i>The King of Stranglers?</i>

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.360
<i>Or the Executioner?</i>

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.360
SHUNKA HIYAMA
WAKASA LIFE INSURANCE COMPANY

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:13.860
Take your stance.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:19.910
Wow!
Remember that stance of Akoya's?

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:25.500
<i>He took it to prevent Kohno's</i>
<i>violent attack in his first game.</i>

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:30.710
<i>Cosmo Imai's choking techniques are</i>
<i>what I have to keep an eye on the most.</i>

00:08:31.550 --> 00:08:33.880
<i>Adam Dudley, whose body type</i>
<i>is similar to mine,</i>

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:36.090
<i>was choked out in a second.</i>

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.600
<i>I should watch out.</i>

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.560
<i>I won't play by your rules.</i>

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:43.520
<i>My strikes will defeat you without fail.</i>

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:45.520
Fight!

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.820
Look at that!

00:08:53.530 --> 00:08:54.400
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:57.530
<i>What are you thinking, Cosmo Imai?</i>

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:01.490
<i>Imai shifted his stance into upright.</i>

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:06.290
<i>Is he going to throw off the grappling</i>
<i>and challenge with a battle of fists?</i>

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:08.920
-What the...
-Hey, seriously?

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:12.300
<i>This game got started</i>
<i>in an unexpected way.</i>

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:18.050
<i>Cosmo Imai, who has the best ground</i>
<i>grappling technique in kengan matches,</i>

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.430
<i>is surprisingly challenging</i>
<i>with a striking fight!</i>

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:22.890
<i>His opponent is Akoya...</i>

00:09:22.970 --> 00:09:24.930
JUN SEKIBAYASHI
HARUO KOHNO (ELIMINATED)

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:28.610
...who perfectly defended against hits
from the over-300 kg monster Kohno.

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:30.070
JERRY TYSON
(ELIMINATED)

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.780
Cosmo, weighing less than 70 kg,

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:36.490
honestly has little chance of winning
with just his fists.

00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:41.790
<i>A jab feint and a low kick in left!</i>

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:44.580
<i>Akoya doesn't lose balance at all!</i>

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.120
<i>Imai doesn't continue and take a distance.</i>

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:50.000
<i>He's so discreet for now.</i>

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.970
<i>A side rolling kick!</i>

00:09:57.090 --> 00:10:02.350
<i>Though he missed, Imai showed us</i>
<i>his brilliant bounce ability!</i>

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:07.810
Does he really think he'll beat
that effing cop only by hitting him?

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:12.980
<i>Here it comes! The Ripper!</i>

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:17.150
<i>Akoya's ripping technique is</i>
<i>to cut the skin by a glancing blow.</i>

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:21.490
<i>Now he used the technique</i>
<i>which afflicted Kohno in his last game!</i>

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:26.120
<i>Look, Imai backs away from Akoya again.</i>

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:30.710
<i>What's wrong with him? We can't see</i>
<i>the usual aggressiveness in him.</i>

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:35.380
<i>That tells us</i>
<i>how cautious he is about Akoya.</i>

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:42.850
<i>Cosmo stopped Akoya's approach!</i>

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:45.270
<i>Now they are inside each other's range!</i>

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:47.850
-He let Cosmo kick him.
-What?

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.440
<i>He's provoking Imai.</i>

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:59.860
<i>Unbelievable.</i>
<i>Imai takes a distance once again!</i>

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:03.200
<i>An air of confusion</i>
<i>is spreading through the venue.</i>

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:07.660
This game could go on forever.

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.080
Kengan matches have no time limit.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.040
And no penalty
for a negative fight, either.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:17.590
Besides, the field is far bigger
than public combat sports.

00:11:18.210 --> 00:11:21.130
You could keep escaping
all day long if you wanted to.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.100
Has this happened before?

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.140
No. The employers won't permit it.

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:30.230
The fighters embody
each company's prestige.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:34.860
If they did such a disgraceful act,
it could hurt the company's reputation.

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:35.900
FIST

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:37.190
What's wrong, Cosmo?

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.280
Show us your more aggressive game!

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.400
Okay.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:43.490
I completed analyzing Cosmo Imai.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.330
Roger.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:48.240
Let's do it, Hiyama.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:51.620
<i>Hmm? Akoya released himself</i>
<i>from the present position.</i>

00:11:55.920 --> 00:11:57.960
<i>Look at that stance!</i>

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:03.300
<i>It looks quite similar to the stance</i>
<i>of the Fang of Metsudo, Agito Kanoh.</i>

00:12:03.930 --> 00:12:04.800
Of course!

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:08.600
We created this stance
inspired by Agito Kanoh.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:12.390
<i>Collecting data from his previous games,</i>

00:12:13.060 --> 00:12:17.730
<i>we refined it to match Akoya's</i>
<i>build, character, and tactics.</i>

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:21.950
<i>It's like a custom-made stance</i>
<i>for Akoya,</i>

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:25.820
<i>more attack-oriented than the original.</i>

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:27.620
<i>It's the fierce assault stance.</i>

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.330
You can't escape anymore.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.290
<i>Cosmo Imai.</i>

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:42.470
<i>You can't escape anymore.</i>

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:44.430
<i>Cosmo Imai.</i>

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.560
Cosmo Imai will evade left
a second later.

00:12:49.680 --> 00:12:51.100
Block him on his right side.

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.230
<i>The painkiller doesn't work, huh?</i>

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:01.990
He'll back up 2.2 meters straight.
Keep close to him.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:05.700
Avoid his straight left by ducking.
Give a right uppercut.

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:07.280
He'll sway to evade it.

00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.240
Left kick to his right leg.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:11.540
<i>Ouch!</i>

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:14.080
Akoya.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.370
Take your time to attack.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:21.050
Cosmo Imai's physical ability
is much poorer than yours.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:23.260
Ruin his mobility. That'll end it.

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:29.220
<i>Let's deprive him of his power</i>
<i>slowly and steadily.</i>

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.060
Damn!

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:35.890
It looks as if the effing cop
can predict Imai's next move!

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:40.400
<i>This man is... incredibly strong!</i>

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:45.860
<i>Kaneda evaded Kaolan's attacks</i>
<i>by predicting his movements.</i>

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:48.030
<i>But this man is...</i>

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:52.330
<i>making his moves after me,</i>
<i>but quicker than me!</i>

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.660
<i>He has outstanding reflexes!</i>

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.920
<i>I've never felt better!</i>

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:04.800
<i>I'm having so much fun</i>
<i>fighting someone as strong as him!</i>

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:08.050
<i>That one hit him for sure.</i>

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:11.430
Hiyama, adjustments need to be made.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.140
<i>Akira, it's as we thought...</i>

00:14:14.270 --> 00:14:16.310
But we still need proof.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.020
Yo, mister!

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:21.150
You cheer Imai on, too!

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:25.990
Yeah, it seems he needs some support.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.910
Akoya, this boy's amazing.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:33.450
It's only by a little,
but his response rate is increasing.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.080
He has tremendous adaptability.

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:41.080
<i>The Ripper is sparking!</i>

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:44.460
<i>He held out amazingly</i>

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:49.050
against your reflexes, the best
among fighters, and my special ability.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.470
Relieve him of his agony now.

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:52.970
Understood!

00:14:56.140 --> 00:14:57.020
<i>He's...</i>

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.770
<i>He's going to finish!</i>

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:00.650
For Cosmo,

00:15:00.770 --> 00:15:03.440
there's no option
but to guard like a turtle!

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:05.440
His center of gravity is low.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:07.360
<i>It's time.</i>

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:09.570
Here we go, Akoya.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.620
<i>The finishing shot!</i>

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.790
<i>The awaited moment of victory!</i>

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:21.960
<i>Entering with no uniform,</i>

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:23.750
<i>a striking battle,</i>

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.300
<i>and a passive approach.</i>

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.260
<i>All of these were bluffing.</i>

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:33.220
<i>Everything was done just for this moment.</i>

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.140
The triangle choke!

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:41.140
Does this mean
that every move he made was...

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:42.730
Just for this?

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.270
Akoya was caught completely unaware!

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:48.940
<i>The tables have turned,</i>
<i>and now Imai has the advantage!</i>

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:51.400
<i>No...</i>

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:55.530
<i>Akoya's scarcely preventing</i>
<i>his being choked!</i>

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:57.790
<i>It can't be true!</i>

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:03.710
<i>My Zone is a counterattack for when</i>
<i>the opponent is only focused on attacking.</i>

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:09.460
<i>No one ever could respond</i>
<i>in less than 0.1 seconds.</i>

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:13.720
<i>This old man...</i>
<i>How crazy are his reflexes?</i>

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:15.890
<i>However,</i>

00:16:16.390 --> 00:16:20.770
<i>something unexpected</i>
<i>was also happening to Akoya.</i>

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:26.690
<i>We investigated the first match and</i>
<i>finished analyzing the mechanism of Zone.</i>

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:32.240
<i>To defeat his Zone, Hiyama sends a signal</i>
<i>at the moment I make an attack.</i>

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.490
<i>Then, I instantly change my focus.</i>

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:40.910
<i>If the timing had been well synchronized,</i>
<i>we could have completely broken the Zone.</i>

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.870
<i>Why was your signal delayed, Hiyama?</i>

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:49.380
You must be thinking that...

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:55.930
it's impossible for me to be here
because you hired skilled guards.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:57.090
Am I right?

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:02.560
<i>You employed many strong men to guard</i>
<i>against attacks from other companies.</i>

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:05.940
<i>But I have good friends, too.</i>

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.100
RYO INABA
(ELIMINATED)

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:09.320
Be on your best behavior, okay?

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:14.570
<i>However strong your guys may be,</i>
<i>no one can react to his sneak attack...</i>

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:17.700
<i>because his main business</i>
<i>is assassination.</i>

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:20.910
The next thing you must be wondering is...

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.830
how your fraud was noticed.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.000
That's quite a simple story.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:31.210
We intercepted
all of your radio transmission.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:35.930
It seems your full attention
was paid to eavesdropping.

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.930
<i>But we have a professional.</i>

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.850
We couldn't get decisive evidence, though.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.480
When did you notice?

00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:49.860
It was just
a strange, little feeling at first.

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:54.900
<i>The way Akoya fought, as if he had</i>
<i>predicted his opponent's moves,</i>

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:57.240
<i>gave me an uncomfortable feeling.</i>

00:17:57.450 --> 00:18:00.620
<i>Then, we made</i>
<i>a thorough investigation of you.</i>

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:06.250
You have an extraordinary ability,
President Hiyama.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:09.750
<i>Your biological clock is quite accurate.</i>

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:14.840
<i>Only a few cases that reach a level</i>
<i>as high as yours exist in the world.</i>

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:20.090
<i>His top-level reflexes,</i>
<i>your unfailing biological clock,</i>

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:21.850
<i>and the discomfort I felt.</i>

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:27.270
These three pieces made it easy
to complete the puzzle.

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.190
President Hiyama.

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:35.480
Even if the truth comes to light,
the Kengan Association won't punish you.

00:18:36.070 --> 00:18:38.610
As long as the referee doesn't find out,

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:41.410
they'll treat the violation
as if it never existed.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:46.160
But the trust in Wakasa Life
Insurance Company would be entirely lost.

00:18:46.660 --> 00:18:49.420
Your future business would be affected.

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.000
Miss Hiyama.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:54.670
Tell Akoya to retire.

00:18:55.170 --> 00:18:58.220
That's my condition
to overlook your injustice.

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:05.100
<i>Despite being in a lock,</i>
<i>Akoya is lifting Cosmo up!</i>

00:19:05.890 --> 00:19:07.220
<i>Ridiculous!</i>

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:08.390
<i>Ridiculous!</i>

00:19:10.270 --> 00:19:12.190
Retire now, Miss Hiyama.

00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:15.480
You have no other choice anymore.

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:18.280
<i>Looks like Nishihonji is blowing his top.</i>

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:20.530
<i>But...</i>

00:19:22.370 --> 00:19:24.240
<i>Cosmo gets behind Akoya!</i>

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.200
<i>Even without a condition like that,</i>

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.410
<i>Cosmo could win!</i>

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:30.540
-Give it back!
-Yo!

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.540
You crazy kimono girl!

00:19:33.960 --> 00:19:35.590
Just give up.

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:39.510
You can't control
your crazy machine anymore.

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:44.890
Still... I can do something.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:45.890
Akoya.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:48.770
So, please...

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.270
<i>Hiyama.</i>

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:52.480
Akoya?

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:56.570
Do you remember what I told you
after our first match?

00:19:57.570 --> 00:19:59.280
After our first match?

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.740
<i>This will be the last time, Hiyama.</i>

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:07.160
<i>Shove off!</i>

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.420
<i>Oh, Cosmo!</i>

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.380
Damn!

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:18.340
<i>Cosmo can't withstand it and escaped!</i>

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.670
<i>The arm's still movable.</i>
<i>No tendons damaged!</i>

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.430
<i>This jerk targeted my eye!</i>

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:29.270
<i>Cosmo's upper body got up.</i>

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:31.020
<i>Akoya's tackle comes instantly!</i>

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:38.440
<i>It's time to enforce justice.</i>

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.820
<i>What? Is he biting?</i>

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:49.580
<i>From Imai's thigh,</i>

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.580
you can see serious bleeding!

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:53.830
Damn!

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.840
What is it with that bastard?
Suddenly, he's even more violent!

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:00.880
What the heck is happening?

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:02.720
Akoya has...

00:21:04.800 --> 00:21:08.140
Akoya has taken the law
into his own hands and executed

00:21:08.470 --> 00:21:12.060
people whom he regards as evil,
calling it the enforcement of justice.

00:21:13.980 --> 00:21:15.900
He does such things underground?

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:19.060
It's called Dirty Harry Syndrome, mister.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.400
That's why I hate cops!

00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:27.570
He's been doing it all to realize
his ideal world where there's no evil.

00:21:29.070 --> 00:21:31.200
<i>His progress was going well.</i>

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:34.410
<i>But the process of fighting evil...</i>

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:37.250
<i>has gradually changed him.</i>

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:40.380
<i>He's been trapped...</i>

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:43.380
<i>in the temptation of murder.</i>

00:21:44.670 --> 00:21:49.430
Since then, he has asked me
for directions in kengan matches...

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:53.770
to avoid getting caught up
in the temptation of murder.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:57.690
You mean you're his brakes?

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:02.230
<i>"Beyond Good and Evil."</i>

00:22:02.690 --> 00:22:04.900
APHORISM NUMBER 146
FROM "BEYOND GOOD AND EVIL"

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:06.070
<i>Aphorism number 146.</i>

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:09.320
<i>"He who fights monsters should beware</i>

00:22:09.820 --> 00:22:13.740
<i>lest he become a monster in the process.</i>

00:22:14.660 --> 00:22:18.000
<i>And when you look long into an abyss,</i>

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:23.800
<i>the abyss also looks back into you."</i>

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:27.300
Oh, gosh!

00:22:27.970 --> 00:22:29.430
Akoya is...

00:22:29.890 --> 00:22:32.260
<i>trapped in the abyss!</i>

00:24:06.020 --> 00:24:06.900
PREVIEW

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:08.820
<i>Is it justice or torture?</i>

00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:10.690
<i>Is fighting equal to killing?</i>

00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:12.700
<i>Beyond redemption!</i>

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:14.370
<i>It's life-or-death.</i>

00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:16.490
<i>Genius versus monster.</i>

00:24:16.950 --> 00:24:18.040
<i>It will be settled.</i>

00:24:18.490 --> 00:24:19.830
<i>Next episode: "Death Match"</i>

00:24:19.950 --> 00:24:21.580
Subtitle translation by
Hinako Someno
